title: 'pallet-broker: fix double counting of re-pooled regions'
doc:
- audience: [Runtime Dev, Runtime User]
  description: |-
    A region pooled with `Provisional` finality could be pooled again, but `do_pool` never
    removed the earlier pooling. The region was counted twice in the pool size, and reassigning
    it afterwards only removed one copy. The leftover share diluted revenue for all other pool
    contributors and could never be claimed.

    `do_pool` now unpools the region before pooling it again, the same way `assign`,
    `partition` and `interlace` already do.

crates:
- name: pallet-broker
  bump: patch
